    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.title": "EUDR Deforestation Verification Pilot",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.subtitle": "Plot-level deforestation-free verification for a Belgian tropical timber importer: four supply origins in Peru, Bolivia and Brazil, one due-diligence report per origin, delivered in 2 of the 5 agreed working days.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.category": "Geospatial / EUDR Compliance",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.location": "Peru · Bolivia · Brazil",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.scale": "27,817 ha verified",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.outcome": "On the pine estate, global data alone would have reported 1,405.6 ha of deforestation. The official Atlantic Forest record confirmed 25.34 ha of native vegetation removal after 2020, in 7 polygons; 1,167.9 ha of the global loss sat in plantation cells, which is harvest, not conversion.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.note": "Client and supplier names are withheld. Figures come from the delivered reports.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.card_desc": "Plot-level EUDR verification for a Belgian timber importer across Peru, Bolivia and Brazil: 27,817 ha checked against PRODES/DETER, JRC TMF and Hansen, with plantation harvest separated from deforestation.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.card_benefit": "On one estate the official record cut 1,405.6 ha of raw global loss to 25.34 ha of real native vegetation removal.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.overview1": "Under the EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR), an importer must show that every plot behind a shipment had no deforestation after 31 December 2020. A Belgian importer of South American tropical timber asked for a four-origin pilot to compare against the verification it was already buying: a natural forest concession in Peru, one in Bolivia, a managed forest unit in the Brazilian Amazon and a pine plantation estate in southern Brazil.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.overview2": "Each origin got its own evidence chain. In Brazil the verdict comes from the official INPE records (PRODES and DETER), checked against the federal rural registry (CAR/SICAR). In Peru and Bolivia two independent global datasets, JRC Tropical Moist Forest and Hansen Global Forest Change, were read straight from public cloud-optimized archives, with no Earth Engine dependency, on a stable 1-hectare grid.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.overview3": "The hard part was not finding loss pixels but deciding which loss counts. Selective logging under an approved management plan and the clear-cut harvest of a planted pine stand both appear as tree-cover loss in global data, yet neither is deforestation under the EUDR. The pipeline separates them, so the report flags conversion, not forestry.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method1": "Validate geometries and CRS (WGS 84 and SIRGAS 2000), match each plot to its CAR receipt and remove duplicated features before any area is counted.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method2": "Brazil: PRODES clear-cut and DETER deforestation from the TerraBrasilis WFS decide the verdict, with coverage proven against the biome mask; DETER degradation, Hansen and TMF stay as context.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method3": "Peru and Bolivia: JRC TMF v1_2025 (deforestation and degradation year) and Hansen GFC v1.13 read by window from public buckets, cut-off after 2020, summarised on a 1 ha grid anchored to the CRS origin.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method4": "Plantation rule: the MapBiomas silviculture class for 2020 is joined to Hansen loss per cell, so harvest and replanting of planted forest is classified as clean.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method5": "Every flagged area checked against dated Sentinel-2 imagery; a revision round moved the Peru and Bolivia flags to review after the imagery showed no conversion.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.method6": "One three-page PDF per origin (verdict per plot, satellite evidence panels, methodology), cross-checked against the JSON outputs before delivery.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.deliverables1": "Four PDF reports, one per origin, ready to attach to the EUDR Due Diligence Statement.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.deliverables2": "Per-cell GeoJSON and CSV results for audit.",
    "cs.eudr-deforestation-verification.deliverables3": "Reproducible Python pipeline that reruns on every PRODES, DETER and JRC update.",
